    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Quantum Algorithm Fixer \u2014 setup (merged final build)\n\n1. Import into n8n at instancey5997 (https://instancey5997.app.n8n.cloud), signed in as zachary@prohm.life via Google SSO. Workflows \u2192 Import from file \u2192 workflow.json.\n2. Run the worker service: `python3 server.py` (venv) on Fartur's Wind. It is exposed to n8n Cloud via Tailscale Funnel at https://farturs-wind.tail44ffde.ts.net and every HTTP node already points there \u2014 do not change the URLs back to localhost.\n3. Google Sheets: the master workbook ('Quantum Algorithm Proof Ledger') is created under the personal Gmail account zacharylafer@gmail.com \u2014 that is the account for the Sheets nodes, NOT the zachary@prohm.life n8n account. The workbook ID is already in both Sheets nodes; just connect the zacharylafer@gmail.com Google account. Per-algorithm tabs are now AUTO-CREATED: the 'Create Algorithm Tab' step calls the Sheets API (spreadsheets.batchUpdate addSheet) after Score and before the appends, so a brand-new algorithm_id gets its own tab on its first run. If the tab already exists the API answers 400 and the step is configured to continue anyway (onError: continueRegularOutput). 'Set Tab URL' reads the new tab's gid from the create response and adds tab_url (ledger URL + #gid=<gid>) and tab_gid to the response record; when the tab already existed, tab_url falls back to the plain ledger URL. Connect the same zacharylafer@gmail.com Google Sheets OAuth2 credential on the 'Create Algorithm Tab' HTTP node too.\n4. POST {\"algorithm_id\": \"grover-3q-v1\", \"algorithm\": \"<OpenQASM 3>\"} to the webhook. The response is the full proof record, now including tab_url and tab_gid.\n\nSim-only: no QPU, no paid services. Simulated today, QPU-ready.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
